{"answer": "**Budget Numbers Thread \u2013 Participants & Commitments**  \n*(Based on the conversation in thread\u202f`thr-group`)*  \n\n| Participant | Email alias (sender_id) | Key commitments made in the thread |\n|-------------|------------------------|------------------------------------|\n| **Alice Ander** | `ct-alice` | \u2022\u202fPromise to post all budget proposals in the thread by **Thursday**.<br>\u2022\u202fStates that the **off\u2011site travel line is already committed** and directs the group to \u201clook at contractors.\u201d|\n| **Bobby** | `ct-bob` | \u2022\u202fQuestions the high travel line and later says the **contractor spend is mainly from the migration project**.<br>\u2022\u202fSaid \u201c**I will take travel scenarios**\u201d and \u201c**right, two renewals we can downgrade.**\u201d|\n| **Carol Corte** | `ct-carol` | \u2022\u202fAgrees with Alice\u2019s comment and asks \u201c**Can we trim the off\u2011site?**\u201d then replies \u201c**I will take tooling.**\u201d |\n| **You** (the assistant) | `ct-self` | \u2022\u202fOffers to \u201c**pull the contractor breakdown tomorrow**.\u201d<br>\u2022\u202fAdds that you will **reconcile** the Q4 numbers against last quarter. |\n\n**Summary of commitments**  \n\n- **Alice** \u2013 Submit proposals by Thursday; keep off\u2011site travel line as is; focus on contractor spend.  \n- **Bobby** \u2013 Handle travel scenarios; downgrade two tooling renewals.  \n- **Carol** \u2013 Take care of tooling renewals.  \n- **You** \u2013 Pull contractor breakdown tomorrow; reconcile Q4 against Q3.", "answer_hash": "48553caa9d31a410c18d85a6e59bb642ba4bb8377fade8dcb22947b073913765", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-16", "seq": 16, "task_id": "t2-group-thread-resolution", "truncated": false, "ts": 1019.0}
